From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Subject: [PATCH] clocksource: ingenic-timer: leave timekeeping to the T41 OST

The T41's TCU channels never get a clock: TER bits stick, TCNT stays
zero, and the TCSR layout is not the T31's, so the timer driver would
register a dead 16-bit sched_clock on top of the OST's working 32-bit one
and freeze every timestamp. Keep the TCU clock provider for the watchdog
and PWM, but stop before registering its clocksource and clockevent when
an `ingenic,t41-ost` node is present.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
---
--- a/drivers/clocksource/ingenic-timer.c
+++ b/drivers/clocksource/ingenic-timer.c
@@ -326,6 +326,20 @@
 					     soc_info->num_channels,
 					     last_bit + 1);
 
+	/*
+	 * Parts with a system OST (the T41) keep time with it: its counter
+	 * is 32 bits wide and already registered as the sched_clock, while
+	 * the TCU channels here are not even clocked. Registering the TCU
+	 * as well would replace that sched_clock with a dead 16 bit one and
+	 * freeze every timestamp. The TCU stays available for PWM and the
+	 * watchdog.
+	 */
+	if (of_find_compatible_node(NULL, NULL, "ingenic,t41-ost")) {
+		pr_info("%s: system OST present, TCU not used for timekeeping\n",
+			__func__);
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	ret = ingenic_tcu_clocksource_init(np, tcu);
 	if (ret) {
 		pr_crit("%s: Unable to init clocksource: %d\n", __func__, ret);
